want to hoard the data to protect

17
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.360
their own career plans. This internal
conflict reveals an even deeper ethical

18
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.140
breach. The team has already collected a
decade's worth of personal patient

19
00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:15.240
data, including occupations and
residential areas, without ever asking for

20
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.240
permission. They operated on a dangerous
assumption that using old hospital

21
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.800
records bypasses the need for research
ethics committee approval or informed

22
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.420
consent. How should a team resolve this
collision between the drive for open

23
00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.960
